# AI Prompts (super-admin editable system / user / format templates)

Editable storage for the prompts powering every AI feature: proofreading, MD generation, **solve-based ANS/SOL generation/checking**, **auto question tagging**, the dashboard **Explain** tutor, the figure-bbox detector, and PDF Batch Import (box detection, anchor/segment detection, and paper-name guess). 33 prompts total. Super-admin only — prompts shape global model behaviour, so the bar is the same as System Settings.

Three pillars:
1. **Variants** — every key supports multiple named variants: one editable **built-in** row (NULL content = registry bootstrap default; reset = null the content, never delete the row) plus admin-created customs. Exactly one variant per key is **active** (the default for unpinned endpoints).
2. **Per-endpoint assignment** — an LLM endpoint can be pinned to a specific variant per key (`prompt_endpoint_assignments`). Unpinned endpoints use the active variant.
3. **Format-rule extraction** — output-formatting rules live in separate `*_FORMAT` items (role `format`), referenced by the spec's `format_key`. They are injected into the system prompt (`system_prompt()`) **and re-appended at the end of the user turn** (`append_format()` under the `OUTPUT FORMAT (mandatory):` header) because some models (GPT builds) under-weight system-role formatting rules.

